MID_NR13_00_m01: <SH>
MID_NR13_00_m01_001: The continent of Fódlan—long has it endured.
MID_NR13_00_m01_002: The goddess above smiles upon that land. But \nnow we turn our eye away from it, across the Lir Sea\nand the Brigid archipelago, to another continent.
MID_NR13_00_m01_003: The land of Dagda. Long ago the goddess entrusted\nit to the Founder Dagda, and it came to be\nknown by his name.
MID_NR13_00_m01_004: He claimed the title of Divine Emperor—and with\nconquest after conquest, forged himself a\nmighty Dagdan Empire.
MID_NR13_00_m01_005: Dagda ruled unchallenged over his land for a\nlong 15 hundred years.
MID_NR13_00_m01_006: There were three vassal states, however, that the\nempire would come to acknowledge, though subject\nto its authority.
MID_NR13_00_m01_007: In the northwest, Arago—founded by the hero Arago,\nwhose veins carried the blood of the Divine\nEmperor. A proud and storied kingdom.
MID_NR13_00_m01_008: In the southwest, Brezarant—founded by the\nchampion Breza, whose veins carried the blood of\nMars, the Bringer of War. A martial kingdom.
MID_NR13_00_m01_009: And still further in the south, Saramis—a younger\nkingdom, and a nation born as a result of a\ncruel fate.
MID_NR13_00_m01_010: Though conflict simmered in these places, Dagda\nas a whole prospered. The empire had been\nenjoying a time of peace.
MID_NR13_00_m01_011: —Saint Cichol, "Dagdan Travels,"\nPart 2, Chapter 1
MID_EV13_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_010_m01_001: Your Majesty... Your Majesty? We're nearly there.
MID_EV13_010_m01_002: Ugh...
MID_EV13_010_m01_003: <NCA>Snap awake.
MID_EV13_010_m01_004: <NCB>Awaken blearily.
MID_EV13_010_m01_005: <ACA>Ah! Pardon me. I must have dozed off.
MID_EV13_010_m01_028: <ACB>
MID_EV13_010_m01_006: I was...dreaming of years ago. Those troubled days\nwhen I took the throne as queen of Saramis.
MID_EV13_010_m01_007: What a mess that was, huh? I'd almost forgot all\nthe chaos and commotion.
MID_EV13_010_m01_008: Bona spent so much time stroking his chin,\nI thought he was gonna pull his beard off.
MID_EV13_010_m01_009: Quite. I was half out of my mind with worry.
MID_EV13_010_m01_010: But it all worked out, thanks to the boss. So for my\nmoney, those are happy memories.
MID_EV13_010_m01_011: For the thousandth time, it's "Your Majesty." Old\nhabits shouldn't die this hard.
MID_EV13_010_m01_012: "It all worked out"? I suppose it did...for now.
MID_EV13_010_m01_013: I hope the long journey did not take its toll on you,\nYour Majesty.
MID_EV13_010_m01_014: We did our all to ride the ocean's currents to make\nthe best time possible.
MID_EV13_010_m01_015: Still, we have traveled far from the royal capital\nof Megaira.
MID_EV13_010_m01_016: All the way up the Sobek River from Fort\nHecatoncheires to Lake Baal, in fact.
MID_EV13_010_m01_017: Not many ships but the Trafalgar could make\nthe voyage.
MID_EV13_010_m01_018: But our voyage is concluded here at Dagsion,\ncapital of the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV13_010_m01_019: <NCA>Take in your surroundings.
MID_EV13_010_m01_020: <NCB>Get moving.
MID_EV13_010_m01_021: <ACA>So this is Dagsion, is it? I've never been before.
MID_EV13_010_m01_022: <ACA>It's everything I heard it was and more.
MID_EV13_010_m01_023: <ACA>If you told me it was the center of the whole world,\nI'd believe you.
MID_EV13_010_m01_024: <ACA>Can't wait to sample the chow they serve here—\nnot to mention the sauce!
MID_EV13_010_m01_025: Our first stop, I think, should be a face-to-face\naudience with this Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_010_m01_026: It was a face beloved by Yu Phas, after all.
MID_EV13_010_m01_027: I have long been interested in taking his measure.
MID_EV13_011_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_011_m01_001: That was merciful of you.
MID_EV13_011_m01_002: How do you figure, Bona? The little punk got decked\npretty good.
MID_EV13_011_m01_003: Yes, but Saraminian law dictates that the guards\nought to have cut the whelp down.
MID_EV13_011_m01_004: By intervening directly, Her Majesty took the\ndecision out of their hands.
MID_EV13_011_m01_005: It was a shrewd move—she managed to spare the\nboy while sticking to protocol.
MID_EV13_011_m01_006: Though...from an outside perspective, she may have\njust gained a reputation for being short-tempered.
MID_EV13_011_m01_007: <NCA>Raise an eyebrow.
MID_EV13_011_m01_008: <NCB>Think back on the boy.
MID_EV13_011_m01_009: <ACA>That said, I think most people will understand.
MID_EV13_011_m01_010: <ACA>You would have been within your rights to kill him,\nbut it may have caused an uproar. You acted wisely.
MID_EV13_011_m01_011: <ACB>It sounds as if you missed a small detail.
MID_EV13_011_m01_012: <ACB>The boy knew enough to roll with the impact of\nmy fist, blunting the blow.
MID_EV13_011_m01_013: <ACB>No ordinary child is so well prepared for combat.
MID_EV13_011_m01_014: <ACB>He kept his wits with you in his face, boss?\nNow that's impressive.
MID_EV13_011_m01_015: A shame to have a blemish on our grand arrival\nin the capital though.
MID_EV13_011_m01_016: I pray it doesn't paint us in a poor light with\nthe temples.
MID_EV13_011_m01_017: I wouldn't worry. We all know the boss has a temper\non her.
MID_EV13_011_m01_018: So don't fret so much, Bona. She handled it well,\nand now we can put it behind us.
MID_EV13_011_m01_019: You really must cease this...this "boss" business.\nIt sets a bad example for the youth.
MID_EV13_011_m01_020: Hah! I didn't realize I was still doing it. Hard to\nthink of her as anything else after so long.
MID_EV13_011_m01_021: All we descendants of Damascar have a complex\nrelationship with the temples.
MID_EV13_011_m01_022: And the temples may be equally wary of us.\nWe ought to be ready for anything.
MID_EV13_011_m01_023: What say you, Bonaventure? Have I conducted\nmyself as a queen should?
MID_EV13_011_m01_024: You are the picture of decorum.
MID_EV13_011_m01_025: {SetColor=Gray}It's odd... Did I truly sense what I thought I did from\nthe boy?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_011_m01_026: {SetColor=Gray}It's as if he bears a burden similar to this arm\nof mine.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_012_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_012_m01_001: We arrived safe in Dagsion today. You honor me\nby granting an audience.
MID_EV13_012_m01_002: I saw a large ship entering the harbor. I wondered\nif it heralded your arrival.
MID_EV13_012_m01_003: That's a long voyage, I believe. I hope you had\nsmooth sailing.
MID_EV13_012_m01_004: <NCA>Be grateful.
MID_EV13_012_m01_005: <NCB>Be modest.
MID_EV13_012_m01_006: <ACA>I am grateful for your hospitality, Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_012_m01_007: <ACA>The rough seas did not trouble us. We are a\nseafaring people of old, after all.
MID_EV13_012_m01_008: <ACB>Thank you for those kind words. I am glad to see you\nin good health, Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_012_m01_009: <ACB>My retainers and I have been marveling at the\nmajesty of Dagsion.
MID_EV13_012_m01_010: It is I who ought to thank you, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_012_m01_011: You have come a long way from Saramis to take\npart in our Heroic Games.
MID_EV13_012_m01_012: All the way from the southern tip of my authority,\nwhere you ward off threats from Southern Dagda.
MID_EV13_012_m01_013: The Mosa there make constant invasion attempts on\nNorthern Dagda.
MID_EV13_012_m01_014: I have heard good things about your efforts on the\nfront line of those conflicts at Fort Zanbar.
MID_EV13_012_m01_015: We owe our peace in no small part to the work\nof your troops.
MID_EV13_012_m01_016: I have always regretted my inability to convey\nmy thanks to you directly.
MID_EV13_012_m01_017: Our peoples may have a complicated history, but I\nhope our relationship stays an amicable one.
MID_EV13_012_m01_018: I hope that as well. Thank you for your consideration\nfor the people of Saramis.
MID_EV13_012_m01_019: Tell me, Queen of Saramis. If you win the\nHeroic Games, what boon will you ask?
MID_EV13_012_m01_020: <NCA>Tell him your desire.
MID_EV13_012_m01_021: I suspect you know already, Lord Solel.
MID_EV13_012_m01_022: My heart's desire is shared by my people.
MID_EV13_012_m01_023: Many kings of Saramis have appealed to the temples\nfor this, but it has never been granted to us.
MID_EV13_012_m01_024: Hm.
MID_EV13_012_m01_025: I wish to annex Cybele, which was once a part of\nthe kingdom of Damascar, as Saramis territory.
MID_EV13_012_m01_026: I would then restore the royal city of Ahm Lu, which\nwas once its capital.
MID_EV13_012_m01_027: And having done that...we seek to rebuild the temple\nof Yu Phas at Ahm Lu.
MID_EV13_012_m01_028: The people of Saramis have long wished for it to\nagain be a holy land and site of worship.
MID_EV13_012_m01_029: I am aware of your pleas—we have not turned our\nback on you. But there is a difficulty.
MID_EV13_012_m01_030: That is a peculiarly dangerous land where the dead\nwalk openly, even in daytime.
MID_EV13_012_m01_031: It has a history I would sooner forget. And so I never\nworked up the resolve to see to its care.
MID_EV13_012_m01_032: But it is gratifying that you and your people\ncontinue to show such devotion to my wife.
MID_EV13_012_m01_033: Should you claim victory in the tournament, I swear\nthat your wish will be granted as best I can.
MID_EV13_012_m01_034: May you find what you seek at the games.
MID_EV13_013_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_013_m01_001: Are those the offspring of the Dagsion prisoners?\nWhat were they, the People of the White Egg?
MID_EV13_013_m01_002: Someone fetch a janitor and tell 'em the temple of\nDagda has been sullied.
MID_EV13_013_m01_003: Rrrr...
MID_EV13_013_m01_004: Oh dear. This could be unpleasant.
MID_EV13_013_m01_005: Bonaventure?
MID_EV13_013_m01_006: This is not the place for it. Do not be goaded,\nYour Majesty.
MID_EV13_013_m01_007: Rrrrrr...
MID_EV13_013_m01_008: What was that faint...cracking sound?
MID_EV13_013_m01_009: Do Saraminians really worship Yu Phas? The Keeper\nof Death and Night?
MID_EV13_013_m01_010: The one who was executed for getting on Dagda the\nGreat's bad side? Must've been some betrayal.
MID_EV13_013_m01_011: What on earth drove the Divine Sovereign to marry\nher? Would've been my last choice, if I was him.
MID_EV13_013_m01_012: Bonaventure?
MID_EV13_013_m01_013: Not. The. Place. Do whatever you must to keep\nyour anger in check while we are here.
MID_EV13_013_m01_014: We are guests of the state. Behaving badly in the\ntemple will reflect poorly on us.
MID_EV13_013_m01_015: We could be ejected from Dagsion, or worse.
MID_EV13_013_m01_016: Give me a shield. Now. Steel, wood—whatever\nyou have!
MID_EV13_013_m01_017: Right away! Here, use mine.
MID_EV13_013_m01_018: Grah!
MID_EV13_013_m01_019: She crushed a shield with her bare hands? Just how\nstrong is this woman?!
MID_EV13_013_m01_020: Strong enough to crumple it into a wad that'd fit\nin your fist!
MID_EV13_013_m01_021: No normal human could do that...
MID_EV13_013_m01_022: Aaah!
MID_EV13_013_m01_023: Enough. Come, Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_014_m01_001: Are you feeling calmer, Your Majesty?
MID_EV13_014_m01_002: You did well to rein yourself in at the temple. I was\npreparing for the worst.
MID_EV13_014_m01_003: Guess we weren't as welcome as we thought.
MID_EV13_014_m01_004: <NCA>Look to Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_014_m01_005: <NCB>Look to Tobias.
MID_EV13_014_m01_006: <ACA>I admit it was a near thing. Another gibe, and I\nmight have plucked their heads from their necks.
MID_EV13_014_m01_007: <ACB>I expected something of the sort. Though it still made\nmy blood boil to hear.
MID_EV13_014_m01_008: That dummy you broke was made of Dagdan oak,\nboss. Takes real power to smash it to splinters.
MID_EV13_014_m01_010: We can expect a certain amount of scorn during our\nstay here, alas.
MID_EV13_014_m01_011: Worship of Yu Phas is seen throughout Dagda as\na minor heresy.
MID_EV13_014_m01_012: Is that not why Your Majesty has made the long\ntrek from Megaira to Dagsion?
MID_EV13_014_m01_013: To restore Yu Phas's good name?
MID_EV13_014_m01_014: <NCA>Nod your assent.
MID_EV13_014_m01_015: Yes. It is as you say.
MID_EV13_014_m01_016: We cannot allow the jeers of the rabble to distract\nus from our holy aim.
MID_EV13_014_m01_017: Dunno what they were hoping to get out of that,\nbut it was more than they bargained for.
MID_EV13_014_m01_018: I got a kick out of watching their faces pale and\ntheir knees knock.
MID_EV13_014_m01_019: Betcha when word of that gets around, we'll hear\na lot fewer snide remarks.
MID_EV13_014_m01_020: Your Majesty, would you care to go for a stroll\naround Dagsion to lighten your mood?
MID_EV13_014_m01_021: Tobias and I will accompany you, naturally.
MID_EV13_014_m01_022: Pardon, but I have little appetite for such things now.
MID_EV13_014_m01_023: Ah, but it would be a shame to miss out on the\ntemple to Yu Phas here.
MID_EV13_014_m01_024: I spoke too soon. I would love to bask in a site so\nconnected to our goddess.
MID_EV13_014_m01_025: We could also visit the temple where Aurora,\nYu Phas's daughter, resides.
MID_EV13_014_m01_026: A splendid idea. We would be remiss not to go and\npay our respects.
MID_EV13_014_m01_027: It is decided. March close and march fast, or I shall\nleave you in my dust!
MID_EV13_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_015_m01_001: Unauthorized persons are not allowed past this point,\nno matter who they are.
MID_EV13_015_m01_002: I am only here to convey my greetings to Aurora.\nPray stand aside.
MID_EV13_015_m01_003: I can't do that. Please leave.
MID_EV13_015_m01_004: <NCA>Ask why not.
MID_EV13_015_m01_005: <NCB>Force your way past.
MID_EV13_015_m01_006: <ACA>Why am I barred from entry? I am a guest of the\nstate, here at the Divine Sovereign's invitation.
MID_EV13_015_m01_007: <ACA>I have told you that my visit here is diplomatic\nin nature.
MID_EV13_015_m01_008: <ACA>Is it given to you to turn such a request away?\nOn what authority?!
MID_EV13_015_m01_009: <ACA>My orders from the Divine Sovereign are that Aurora\nis to see no one.
MID_EV13_015_m01_010: <ACB>Aurora is the daughter of Yu Phas, to whom we owe\nmuch. I will meet with her, and you will not stop me!
MID_EV13_015_m01_011: <ACB>This is a public temple. I ask that you please\nwithdraw before you make a scene.
MID_EV13_015_m01_012: You insolent—
MID_EV13_015_m01_013: Easy there, boss!
MID_EV13_015_m01_014: Please, Your Majesty, try to calm yourself.
MID_EV13_015_m01_015: There seem to be reasons we are not privy to. Let us\ngo elsewhere for now and return later.
MID_EV13_015_m01_016: <NCA>Withdraw.
MID_EV13_015_m01_017: Very well. My apologies.
MID_EV13_015_m01_018: You know, I once heard a strange rumor about\nthis temple.
MID_EV13_015_m01_019: They say that people disappear from here\non occasion.
MID_EV13_015_m01_020: Yeah, I thought I heard some folks inside mention\nsomething like that.
MID_EV13_015_m01_021: But what do they mean by "disappear"? They think\nthe ones who vanish are still alive?
MID_EV13_015_m01_022: Thorough investigations have been performed,\nbut it is still a mystery.
MID_EV13_015_m01_023: The Divine Sovereign cast some suspicion on Aurora\nand forbade her from leaving the temple.
MID_EV13_015_m01_024: That is surprising. Aurora is the Divine Sovereign's\ndaughter. Why would he confine her?
MID_EV13_015_m01_025: Who can say? But I would guess we're being turned\naway due to the disappearances.
MID_EV13_015_m01_026: Then he mistrusts his own daughter?
MID_EV13_015_m01_027: Your Majesty, we have not yet been to the temple\nof Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_015_m01_028: It is one of her minor temples, but Yu Phas did\nspend time there in person once.
MID_EV13_015_m01_029: Shall we visit? It may help to clear your mood.
MID_EV13_015_m01_030: I am reminded of when I snuck into the temple of\nYu Phas at Cybele when I was a child.
MID_EV13_015_m01_031: But that temple was in ruins—a mere shell of its\nformer glory.
MID_EV13_015_m01_032: Your Majesty! If the temples knew you had snuck\ninto Cybele, you could be accused of high crimes.
MID_EV13_015_m01_033: Worry not. That was long ago, and there were\nno witnesses.
MID_EV13_015_m01_034: Now then, let us hasten to the temple of Yu Phas!
MID_EV13_015_m01_035: 
MID_EV13_016_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_016_m01_001: A minor obstacle.
MID_EV13_016_m01_002: Your Majesty! It is not so minor for everyone!
MID_EV13_016_m01_003: We're not so young anymore, boss!
MID_EV13_016_m01_004: Save your breath. I expect better of my retainers.\nKeep up, or I shall find new ones.
MID_EV13_016_m01_005: Quick, Bona, what's the plan?
MID_EV13_016_m01_006: Don't panic! Perhaps there is a flaw we can exploit,\nor at least a crate we can stand on...
MID_EV13_016_m01_007: The point is there must be a way! And it's up to\nus to find it—quickly!
MID_EV13_016_m01_008: Yeah! That's what makes you the best tactician in\nSaramis. C'mon, let's get to it.
MID_EV13_016_m01_009: Those two.
MID_EV13_016_m01_010: So...this is Yu Phas. She's as resplendent as\nI imagined.
MID_EV13_016_m01_011: <NCA>Gaze at the statue.
MID_EV13_016_m01_012: Haah...
MID_EV13_016_m01_013: It was learning of Yu Phas which first made me\nconsider that one day I would be queen.
MID_EV13_016_m01_014: Boss, we did it! We finally...caught up!
MID_EV13_016_m01_015: We climbed a nearby tree, allowing us to clear the\nwall. That's going to take a toll on these bones...
MID_EV13_016_m01_016: Well, well! I see you've found a sculpture of Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_016_m01_017: I wonder if it's the work of the legendary Shandor,\nas the ones in the other temples are.
MID_EV13_016_m01_018: Oh, it appears to be a genuine original, and not a\nlater work by one of his apprentices.
MID_EV13_016_m01_019: They say he could carve marble so finely as to\nreproduce the drape of wet silk.
MID_EV13_016_m01_020: I suspect this statue accurately depicts the face of\nYu Phas while she yet lived.
MID_EV13_016_m01_021: There was a statue in the temple at Cybele as well.\nBut its face had unfortunately been chiseled off.
MID_EV13_016_m01_022: This is the first time I've beheld her face, even\nthrough the hand of a sculptor.
MID_EV13_016_m01_023: I feel...moved to tears at the sight of it.
MID_EV13_016_m01_024: Pardon, but might I have a moment alone?
MID_EV13_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_018_m01_001: Hm?
MID_EV13_018_m01_002: That's the one I met in the mist... The one who gave\nme that strange sand!
MID_EV13_018_m01_003: Halt! I have questions for you!
MID_EV13_018_m01_004: Oh!
MID_EV13_018_m01_005: No sign of them. Where could they have vanished to?
MID_EV13_018_m01_006: Where did you come from?!
MID_EV13_018_m01_007: Ah!
MID_EV13_018_m01_008: Who are you? What are you doing in here?!
MID_EV13_018_m01_009: Oh! Are you a thief?
MID_EV13_018_m01_012: Hardly! Besides, you're far more suspicious looking\nthan I.
MID_EV13_018_m01_013: OK, well... Maybe you're not a thief, but ordinary\ncitizens need special permission to enter the temples.
MID_EV13_018_m01_014: Then what of you? Surely we are both guilty of\ntrespassing.
MID_EV13_018_m01_015: Oh, no, I'm temple staff. See? I have the mark of\na lead priest right here.
MID_EV13_018_m01_016: A priest, then. I'll have you know I am no "ordinary\ncitizen," as you put it.
MID_EV13_018_m01_017: I am Theodora Sergio Savangren, queen of Saramis.
MID_EV13_018_m01_018: You're a queen? I wish I could trust you on that,\nbut I just don't know.
MID_EV13_018_m01_019: This talk of trust is laughable coming from behind\nthat ridiculous mask.
MID_EV13_018_m01_020: Now you're being rude. Ridiculous?
MID_EV13_018_m01_021: There are important reasons why I can't take my\nmask off. Not for you, not for anyone.
MID_EV13_018_m01_024: {SetColor=Gray}Very odd that she refuses to show her true face in\na temple... Is she a criminal after all?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_018_m01_025: {SetColor=Gray}I've never heard of a masked priest.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_018_m01_026: {SetColor=Gray}Or have I? It does ring faintly familiar, now that\nI stop to think.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_018_m01_027: Never mind that. Answer me this first.
MID_EV13_018_m01_028: Did you see a stranger come this way? A shadowy\nperson clad in white?
MID_EV13_018_m01_029: A shadowy person? Wearing white?
MID_EV13_018_m01_030: A clear no, then. Could it have been an apparition?
MID_EV13_018_m01_031: Shhh! I heard a noise from that way.
MID_EV13_018_m01_032: What? I didn't hear anything.
MID_EV13_018_m01_033: Hey, are you sure there's treasure here?
MID_EV13_018_m01_034: Sure I'm sure. The place is a dump now, but a god\nlived here once.
MID_EV13_018_m01_035: Take that picture there! It's a little faded, but it's\ngotta be worth something.
MID_EV13_018_m01_036: Even if it isn't, we could live for months off selling\nthe divinium frame!
MID_EV13_018_m01_037: Stop where you are! Thieves, all of you!
MID_EV13_018_m01_038: There really were thieves? Your ears must be trained\nindeed to have heard them.
MID_EV13_018_m01_039: Boss! We've been made! Wh-what do we do?!
MID_EV13_018_m01_040: What are witnesses doing in this run-down temple?!\nWell, only one thing to do.
MID_EV13_018_m01_041: Take 'em out so we can ditch this place!
MID_EV13_019_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_019_m01_001: Un... Unbelievable...
MID_EV13_019_m01_002: Of all the luck...running into those terrors...
MID_EV13_019_m01_003: That takes care of that. I'll hand these thieves over\nto the temple knights.
MID_EV13_019_m01_004: You can leave the rest to me!
MID_EV13_019_m01_005: I...I see. You do seem quite capable. I will leave this\nin your hands.
MID_EV13_019_m01_006: Oh! But I was serious when I said this place is off-\nlimits to ordinary citizens.
MID_EV13_019_m01_007: I'll ignore it this time, since you helped me out.\nBut rules are rules!
MID_EV13_019_m01_008: I can muster no excuse. As you say, I will take\nmy leave.
MID_EV13_019_m01_009: But before I go, cat-masked priest... What is\nyour name?
MID_EV13_019_m01_010: Oh...I'm Orchel, with Credna's temple.
MID_EV13_019_m01_011: Hmm...
MID_EV13_019_m01_012: I can't put my finger on it, but there's something\nfamiliar about her.
MID_EV13_019_m01_013: Somehow both reassuring and...frightening.\nShe might be dangerous...
MID_EV13_069_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_069_m01_001: I've noticed you don't take kindly to orders these\ndays, boss.
MID_EV13_069_m01_002: But you didn't pitch a fit when that girl scolded you.
MID_EV13_069_m01_003: You're right... I wonder why that is.
MID_EV13_069_m01_004: The young maiden was an enigma even aside from\nher mask.
MID_EV13_069_m01_005: <NCA>Consider this.
MID_EV13_069_m01_006: Perhaps that very air of mystery distracted me from\nmy irritation.
MID_EV13_069_m01_007: {SetColor=Gray}This year is 1449 by the Imperial Calendar. If Troy\nis to be believed...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_069_m01_008: {SetColor=Gray}I have another seven years, at best, of sanity.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV13_069_m01_009: What was that about seared pests, boss? I could go\nfor some stick bugs myself!
MID_EV13_069_m01_010: They do 'em fried up here, and they're incredible.\nThough I like 'em stewed too.
MID_EV13_069_m01_011: Haaah...
MID_EV13_069_m01_012: Hm. The masked priest reminded me of something.
MID_EV13_069_m01_013: It's a story Troy once told me.
MID_EV13_069_m01_014: Yu Phas also spent much of her life concealing her\nface with a mask.
MID_EV13_069_m01_015: Only after marrying Solel and entering the Dagda\npantheon did she remove it.
MID_EV13_069_m01_016: <NCA>Ask for details.
MID_EV13_069_m01_017: <NCB>Pay this no heed.
MID_EV13_069_m01_018: <ACA>I would hear more, Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_069_m01_019: <ACA>Ahem. This is a tale from an age long before the\nkingdom of Damascar was formed.
MID_EV13_069_m01_020: <ACA>It was told originally by a caretaker who delivered\nfood to the Isle of Balor.
MID_EV13_069_m01_021: <ACA>According to the story, the four daughters of Balor\nwatched over the island's temple.
MID_EV13_069_m01_022: <ACA>All of them hid behind ominous masks, never\nshowing their true faces.
MID_EV13_069_m01_023: <ACA>The tale does not relate why they did this.
MID_EV13_069_m01_024: <ACA>Yes, I believe I have heard this one. Though I had\nforgotten it until now.
MID_EV13_069_m01_025: <ACA>The goddess Yu Phas was one of those four sisters—\na daughter of Balor.
MID_EV13_069_m01_026: <ACA>But the tale makes no mention of their masks being\ncat shaped, or of them possessing uncanny strength.
MID_EV13_069_m01_027: So the connection to our masked maiden seems\ntenuous at best.
MID_EV13_069_m01_028: Hm. And yet, it was within the temple of Yu Phas\nthat I met our enigmatic priest.
MID_EV13_069_m01_029: Even if it is coincidence, I am uneasy.
MID_EV13_069_m01_030: A mask that must never be removed...